      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 27, 2018 7:53:43 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Few more pics before the month turns.  About to get these guys out of the greenhouse since we are due for some upper 70s next week though the plan is being crimped for the weekend as we'll probably have a frost advisory Saturday night.  Beating a dead horse, but gotta love Midwest springs.<br/><br/>Cuprea (Ornata Gulf Coast x Cuprea Lois)<br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://urqk2a.by.files.1drv.com/y4mUvjzNduddIk-KczSg008hmt8JL7qv1rfQpihbzKjqFudPqLDwSMQjVi4fUr3_Xoe4UdBF81hPyBNDJgwD4A2gMiwj5pY4-WWB5KjDX-xo01GjJic3IuZeZfzKl8CNPL5KcEKAXFemWwIDvoWtEr0jY375OrntGS9XNYuhlilcB6tbTcXKmNKJSDralS8JpP3Zl9BYxTKLc9f0ES_SIjJhA?width=495&amp;height=660&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/>Alata Red/Black x Flava Kimber - <br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://fyorzg.by.files.1drv.com/y4mGseZbX959qytVGeCsOoA6_YGCgggg-QilF1nzLnTA93HKanFOP5nbNf66Kd3OcwYxubBPvVM9NbVP34Wy9O8nOQncPtRb3qY0DE_hrw-RQnSfVxAe87dRMRh5oHJx6nYURaN3v26s5qSyboO7zbaUsMX4cN-EpouVFJ8Zx-BjZ1y9IzroDbfskDhWgA_ZwbWp5aUaIx8aMYJ0hGVxHEkOA?width=495&amp;height=660&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/>Leucophylla x Flava Rugelii - <br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://vs9pew.by.files.1drv.com/y4mAF-bOzqo2v7Yt_m9Lqn2DmkEtURWH5W39izWENWxO8VRywgVuK0X93JRZtdN8tvEQpOLahXonFf4_5HKZivSDpqLhVulbb0iJQorxgusdTOztkzXleVuYFEW-sJ3-OPMCwS4F6IO1Mor82e2RKbbvqlxLNk43t1tJ-svioGsAHcGgu5J9eVS4ayeer7rLae4P0clz6OAYmb7HhUsBUhG-w?width=495&amp;height=660&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/>Bird's Beak Flower<br/><br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://urqn2a.by.files.1drv.com/y4mIufH9XmvSyW-yWclU1-p2H8xXRsCZtWV6euHSyp7HDVKAmN-RsvJvWMwBCUC71cvoYCtSs2UDqDalY-UKBfMyW4dP4WHmKNLjfOvWtAjYcU_8ZlFafPK0nbTOogMnF9l2rwRDA39WjpD9BFgVWOcDjznS10hxObIChq6kectkn83iyVpNOO-j9T3Q6gwq3L1gZldZJ8zLTiV_nTSg_LH9A?width=495&amp;height=660&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/>flava var. ornata 'improved black veins' - just received this spring so has a ways to go, but I can already see how awesome this variety is, the shape of the pitcher just stands out!<br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://sbqu2a.by.files.1drv.com/y4mNP0QHhvBdGdhLmVo24w2W2xefPKwWAR4Y3I1dxaUTER-BWW4V-BqOCop10kX_at3uGgdMJ8weh0RSUipnZOz2xhqePScGSe3PhF9d9ThyuJ69G_gPzyKbLsztudaHw8xsOTpqzfa-1tgC2Sr-x3X3DkUrT9FcZwHb-igcWsb_QkK7MHlJO-3gq25deHak1c2pHoiYFZCT3MLUwxl4AinQw?width=495&amp;height=660&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/>And lastly, outdoor bog being doubled in size and depth, ready for some transplanting in May!  Time to decide what lucky specimens get to be treated to Ohio winters.<br/><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://vs9oew.by.files.1drv.com/y4m3jTPaInlZhqRHojXKMee5e1AXwBSDoq4eufSXgUnguRJ9oIaXEgc11i0mhdxO7AIhUYNv1_ClwxfyoStjd8AGB8QCwiL7ZqBQESclnfKWmkHu_CfeZi9QXkCpwwqWZnc45WgnmXZ0HuA2plk0HJxc92yEHqk7kdyjG7kJWw_5erLajTRbtTYptJp4S_h-UfBOSJrcFLb08kvenYL1fc5rg?width=660&amp;height=495&amp;cropmode=none\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>",
      "body_text": "Few more pics before the month turns.  About to get these guys out of the greenhouse since we are due for some upper 70s next week though the plan is being crimped for the weekend as we'll probably have a frost advisory Saturday night.  Beating a dead horse, but gotta love Midwest springs.\nCuprea (Ornata Gulf Coast x Cuprea Lois)\nAlata Red/Black x Flava Kimber -\nLeucophylla x Flava Rugelii -\nBird's Beak Flower\nflava var. ornata 'improved black veins' - just received this spring so has a ways to go, but I can already see how awesome this variety is, the shape of the pitcher just stands out!\nAnd lastly, outdoor bog being doubled in size and depth, ready for some transplanting in May!  Time to decide what lucky specimens get to be treated to Ohio winters.",
